ALIS
Automated Lecturer & Institutional System
Technical Architecture & Product Specification
Version: 1.0
Prepared for: Engineering Leadership (CTO / Senior Developers)
Author: QUAICU

1. Executive Overview
ALIS (Automated Lecturer & Institutional System) is an AI-assisted institutional operating system designed for universities.

Traditional university ERPs act as passive record-keeping systems. They store data but require humans to perform most operational and intellectual tasks.

ALIS is fundamentally different.

It is designed as an active institutional engine capable of:

• generating academic artifacts
• analyzing institutional data
• enforcing policy constraints
• orchestrating workflows
• automating operational decisions
• maintaining full governance and audit integrity

However, AI in ALIS never directly controls the system.
All final decisions are enforced by deterministic institutional logic.

This ensures the system remains:

• legally auditable
• deterministic
• policy-compliant
• enterprise-safe

2. Core Philosophy
ALIS is built around four fundamental principles.

2.1 AI Is Advisory, Not Authoritative
AI may:

• analyze
• suggest
• generate drafts
• extract information

AI may NOT:

• mutate database state
• execute irreversible operations
• bypass policy rules
• override authority

2.2 Deterministic Governance
All institutional decisions are governed by:

• policy registry
• rule engine
• state machine
• authority enforcement

This guarantees deterministic behavior.

2.3 Replayable Institutional History
Every action in ALIS must be reproducible.

This is achieved by logging:

• model version
• prompt version
• policy version
• inputs
• outputs
• actor identity

This enables complete forensic replay of institutional decisions.

2.4 Modular Institutional Architecture
Universities operate across multiple domains.

ALIS is therefore organized into independent modules, each responsible for a domain of institutional operations.

Modules communicate through event-driven orchestration.

3. ALIS Functional Scope
ALIS currently contains 8 modules and 77 operational wizards.

Each wizard represents a specific operational capability.

